  "Featured Snippets": "Featured snippets are the one metric that has moved clearly backward: starting at 287, climbing to a high of 396 in March, then falling sharply through Q2 to settle in the 109–148 range. A snippet-recovery push — schema markup, answer-box formatting, definition-style content — should be a near-term priority alongside the ranking wins elsewhere.",
  "Website Performance Score": "Desktop performance has drifted down from a 68 baseline to the mid-50s most weeks (currently 59), while mobile has held roughly flat (48 → 33 most recently). Both scores bounce week to week, typical of PageSpeed measurements, but the desktop softening warrants a technical health check given its direct link to Core Web Vitals.",
  "Core Web Vitals": "Both desktop and mobile Core Web Vitals have logged a Fail status in every measured week since tracking began. This is the single most important technical item in this report: Core Web Vitals are a confirmed Google ranking factor, and a sustained Fail status is a ceiling on how far the ranking gains elsewhere can go. A CWV remediation sprint (LCP, INP, CLS) should be prioritized immediately.",
  "Search-Generated Engagement (AI Overviews)": "This is the standout growth story in the report. AI Overview keyword presence (SEMrush) has grown from 13,887 to 22,905 — up 65% versus baseline. Citation counts across every major AI assistant have grown in parallel: ChatGPT citations peaked near 13,000 in June (from 8,862), Gemini is up to 1,548 (from 1,237), and Claude citations have nearly doubled from 179 to 370 after peaking above 570. Fortinet's content is clearly earning a growing share of voice inside AI-generated answers.",
